{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1028781-are-sidereals-regular-reincarnations","id":1028781,"title":"Are Sidereals regular-reincarnations?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Sidereal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-08T17:19:44-08:00","id":1028781,"title":"Are Sidereals regular-reincarnations?","content":"Something occurred to me when thinking about how Sidereal Exaltations work:<br /> <br /> Unlike other Celestials, Sidereal reincarnation works <i>exactly</i> like regular soul-reincarnation. It's set from birth, and the new incarnation has to be born after the old one dies.<br /> <br /> So... is there any particular reason why Sidereal Exaltations shouldn't be permanently bound to a particular upper soul (in, unlike other Celestials, a bond that transcends death?) Having two kinds of reincarnation always bothered me (it tends to make it feel like Celestials aren't &quot;real&quot; reincarnations), and it occurred to me that there's no particular reason why Sidereal Exaltations can't reincarnate in both ways, since their Exaltations already behave as if they do in every way that matters.<br /> <br /> (This would imply that Sidereals are immune to the small number of effects that can destroy an upper soul or interfere with its reincarnation, but that is not a particularly big deal - it means you can never have Alchemicals who had a past life as a Sidereal, I guess.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T17:33:37-08:00","id":1028791,"title":"","content":"I think the biggest thing that is odd about that is that if they're tied in that fashion, then you can't have a ghost of a Sidereal meet the inheritor of their Exaltation. And there's probably some plot element sin there that are being missed if an Exaltation can't manifest unless its soul moves along.<br /> <br /> I think as a note what helps a lot is not calling Celestial Exaltation a form of reincanration but a form instead of legacy. You aren't an incarnation of some other Exalted. You're their successor. You're the next element in the legend of that Exaltation in a sense. Just like your predecessor also was a contributor to that particular legend. If that makes any sense.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T17:46:04-08:00","id":1028800,"title":"","content":"Oh, that's right... this would mean that either Sidereals couldn't leave ghosts, or their reincarnation would be delayed until the ghost chose to reincarnate. I guess that wouldn't work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T17:49:29-08:00","id":1028803,"title":"","content":"Hmmm... is attaching Exaltations to specific souls something Saturn would go for? It both does and <i>doesn't</i> fit the image of Endings as a process of renewal, depending on how you look at it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T18:09:03-08:00","id":1028807,"title":"","content":"Sids have a 5 thousand year life span and then they die, as a retirement plan. (I will admit I once speculated with a friend on the idea of Sids actually having a longer natural lifespan, but no one wants to stick around past retirement age.) Honestly, I would think it kind of cruel to be reborn to the same post the very next life with a break of ,what, 80 years on the upper limit if we assume someone got fated to exalt on their death bed of old age. <br /> <br /> Though I think another thing to consider is that fate isn't exactly a solid thing. I mean literally part of the Sid job is either ensuring fate/destiny doesn't go off the rails or forcing it to if the outcome is undesirable. So fating a person to exalt sidereal still requires they live long enough to see their destiny and the number of things walking around Creation that will screw up a destiny on a whim or accident in Creation is terrifying. If you bound a Sidereal exaltation to a single soul not just a single destiny, but a single soul that could cause serious damage by just making sure to track a person's reincarnations down and killing them every time they reincarnate. Indeterminate time for reincarnation and it could be easy or only a tricky bit to keep a bunch of sids out of circulation for centuries on end. <br /> <br /> Though the reckoning at the end when the Sids find out who the jerk is that's been making them even more horribly understaffed than normal would be glorious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T21:30:29-08:00","id":1028867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1028781-are-sidereals-regular-reincarnations#post1028781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having two kinds of reincarnation always bothered me (it tends to make it feel like Celestials aren't &quot;real&quot; reincarnations),</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess maybe? But aren't the plot hooks this makes possible really delicious in a lot of ways?<br /> <br /> I mean... there are thirteen Solars/Abyssals/Infernals out there who bear the Exaltations once held by Deathlords. Tell me <i>that</i> doesn't open up a whole realm of possibilities, and that is just off the top of my head.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T22:32:20-08:00","id":1028883,"title":"","content":"Somehow I'm fundamentally uncomfortable with the idea of ghosts with Sidereal Charms being a regular possibility, both from a lore, mechanics, and setting-impact perspective.<br /> <br /> Also, the &quot;successor&quot; and &quot;no I like my current life more&quot; stories are meaningfully different but equally fun for Sidereals relative to other Exalt types, and while normally I vote for lots of diversity, this feels like it blocks off more potential stories than it opens up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12682-remedy","name":"Remedy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T00:49:06-08:00","id":1028916,"title":"","content":"I like the idea that the Maidens use multifarious tools from life to life, and the nature of a Sidereal Exalt can be sharply different from life to life. That fits less to me with a single soul, where I feel like there's more of an expectation of single personhood. Fate and destiny seem like they should be inherently flexible in their means.<br /> <br /> It also makes the &quot;5000 years and when you're fated to die, and that's that&quot; bite differently, if your soul will rise again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T03:15:54-08:00","id":1028941,"title":"","content":"The nature and memories that come with the Essence remain absent until the time of actual Exaltation, don't they?<br /> <br /> \u200bI prefer the idea that the Sidereal Exaltation, even if bestowed at birth, is not attached to the reincarnating soul because it allows for a greater range of personalities to be Exalted.<br /> <br /> \u200bWithin the conceits that I attach to normal reincarnation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T23:02:45-08:00","id":1029486,"title":"","content":"Ya know despite the problems with the idea that Blaque mentioned, and my general dislike of changing anything about Sidereals at all (except Paradox, per that thread I started a while ago). I kinda like this idea. It certainly bears some thought, and wouldn't necessarily be bad for a one-off character (as long as no one tries to take it to Mary Sue levels of 'specialness'). I'll have to give this some more thought in the morning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12167-broken-masque","name":"Broken Masque","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T02:26:58-08:00","id":1029515,"title":"","content":"I like it, because I like the idea of your previous incarnation <i>being your previous incarnation</i>. I feel it makes the previous incarnation more meaningful.<br /> But... yeah, it does mean that if a Sidereal becomes a ghost for, say, 300 years, there's no Sidereal to replace them, and I think that's an issue as it'll mean there's even less Sidereals than there are now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T14:44:35-08:00","id":1030806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1028781-are-sidereals-regular-reincarnations?p=1029515#post1029515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like it, because I like the idea of your previous incarnation <i>being your previous incarnation</i>. I feel it makes the previous incarnation more meaningful.<br /> But... yeah, it does mean that if a Sidereal becomes a ghost for, say, 300 years, there's no Sidereal to replace them, and I think that's an issue as it'll mean there's even less Sidereals than there are now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, that gives a nice story hook for other sidereals and a reason to go into the Underworld: go &quot;convince&quot; that powerful Exalted's ghost to reincarnate, their vacation time ran out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T18:38:48-08:00","id":1030920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1028781-are-sidereals-regular-reincarnations?p=1028800#post1028800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, that's right... this would mean that either Sidereals couldn't leave ghosts, or their reincarnation would be delayed until the ghost chose to reincarnate. I guess that wouldn't work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, Exaltations bind themselves to the lower soul. That's been cited as a reason why their hungry ghosts are so pants-shittingly terrifying in the text, even.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T19:21:50-08:00","id":1030959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1028781-are-sidereals-regular-reincarnations?p=1030920#post1030920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, Exaltations bind themselves to the lower soul. That's been cited as a reason why their hungry ghosts are so pants-shittingly terrifying in the text, even.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that could work differently for Sidereals, as far as that goes. It even makes thematic sense given that they're one of the more &quot;intellectual&quot; types of Exalted; Solars and Lunars are (broadly) chosen for their passions and the things those passions ignite in them, whereas Sidereals are chosen according to a plan from before they were born.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T19:47:28-08:00","id":1030972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1028781-are-sidereals-regular-reincarnations?p=1030806#post1030806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, that gives a nice story hook for other sidereals and a reason to go into the Underworld: go &quot;convince&quot; that powerful Exalted's ghost to reincarnate, their vacation time ran out.</div> </div> </div> </div>For good or for ill, making the Underworld serve as the Sidereal Vacation Home ties them more to that setting.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I feel like the base Sidereal narrative already drives home that Fate is monstrous, heartless, utterly unconcerned with individual happiness (or that of the masses), and yet Sidereals are beholden to keeping it running. The knowledge that you're stuck in a job for the rest of your life, you only get to retire upon death, and that whenever you reincarnate (spoiler: unless you have unfinished business you're likely to do that quite quickly) you're going to start the whole mess over again strikes me as the sort of thing that would lead to tremendous Sidereal job dissatisfaction. I mean, it's not like they remember their past incarnations, but the knowledge that it never ends for them, <i>never</i>, is just...kind of soul-crushing.<br /> <br /> Speaking of, souls are destructible. They can be soulforged and obliterated and likely unmade in other ways. Binding an exaltation to something so fragile--unless it empowers their ghosts, which opens up a whole new terrible starmetal can of worms--seems pretty unwise.<br /> <br /> You could theoretically argue that this was a decision made before the Underworld was a thing, but that's the kind of explanation I'm not sure I care for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T19:59:48-08:00","id":1030979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1028781-are-sidereals-regular-reincarnations?p=1030972#post1030972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For good or for ill, making the Underworld serve as the Sidereal Vacation Home ties them more to that setting.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I feel like the base Sidereal narrative already drives home that Fate is monstrous, heartless, utterly unconcerned with individual happiness (or that of the masses), and yet Sidereals are beholden to keeping it running. The knowledge that you're stuck in a job for the rest of your life, you only get to retire upon death, and that whenever you reincarnate (spoiler: unless you have unfinished business you're likely to do that quite quickly) you're going to start the whole mess over again strikes me as the sort of thing that would lead to tremendous Sidereal job dissatisfaction. I mean, it's not like they remember their past incarnations, but the knowledge that it never ends for them, <i>never</i>, is just...kind of soul-crushing.<br /> <br /> Speaking of, souls are destructible. They can be soulforged and obliterated and likely unmade in other ways. Binding an exaltation to something so fragile--unless it empowers their ghosts, which opens up a whole new terrible starmetal can of worms--seems pretty unwise.<br /> <br /> You could theoretically argue that this was a decision made before the Underworld was a thing, but that's the kind of explanation I'm not sure I care for.</div> </div> </div> </div>While it's being de-emphasized this edition Sids do remember their prior incarnations. Heck the 2E book said that for various reasons Sids remember their prior incarnations more than the other exalt types, to the point where some occasionally end up torn over the decision to overthrow the Primordials. (And not in the &quot;In hindsight was that really a good idea&quot; way.) <br /> <br /> Like Mockery says certain aspects like soul steel or having your higher soul anihilated as a ghost probably weren't considered do to not being around, but 100 people with the eternal drudgery of knowing that the only way out of their job is death and even then only for vacation purposes would be insane. I mean Rakan Thulio stops being the big rogue Sid and starts being the only one of these people I can understand at that point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T19:06:43-08:00","id":1033809,"title":"","content":"Since doing a bunch of Exalted reading on reincarnation for a Sidereal character concept I've come around believing this is true. I'm not certain it's canon, though you do see text that in places that talks as if it is (&quot;The Sidereals work to safeguard the birth of their spiritual sibling and to ensure that the conditions are right, according to the pattern of destiny. Thereafter, they keep a close watch on the newly incarnated Sidereal soul, typically from afar, gently guiding and safeguarding it until the time is right for that spirit to Exalt once more.&quot;, Sidereal 1E, page 84)<br /> <br /> What convinced me was that it fit completely with the Perfected Hierarchy in Immaculate metaphysics. Of course the Bronze Sidereals would write a religion where a soul reincarnating again and again as an Exalt is a sign of wisdom and enlightenment!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1564-shinjo","name":"Shinjo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}